{title: Kingdom of God}
{subtitle: Acts 28:11–31}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] | [Cm] |
| [Cm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Three months passed [Eb]on the island shore
[Bb]We put to sea in Ale[Cm]xandria's hold
Twin Brothers [Eb]on the bow we saw
[Bb]Syracuse and Rhegium [Cm]on the road
Puteoli brothers [Eb]welcomed us home
[Bb]Seven days we stayed be[Cm]fore we roam
To Rome where the Forum [Eb]of Appius stood
[Bb]Paul saw them and thanked God for his [Cm]blood
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Ab]He was allowed [Eb]to live with his guard
[Bb]Three days later the leaders [Cm]came to the yard
[Ab]He said I did nothing [Eb]against our fathers
Yet [Bb]I was handed over to [G]Caesar's doors
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Cm]I am wearing this chain for [Eb]the hope of Israel
[Bb]Laying out the kingdom [Cm]of God before us
From morning until eve[Eb]ning he spoke the truth
Convinc[Bb]ing some while others re[G]mained in the [Cm]booth
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
They had no letters [Eb]from Judea to show
[Bb]Nor bad reports from the broth[Cm]ers below
But they wanted to hear what he [Eb]thought of the sect
[Bb]Spoken against in every [Cm]part of the net
So they set a day and came in crowds great [Eb]
To his lodg[Bb]ing where the [Cm]light was late
From Moses and Prophets he [Eb]tried to persuade
About [Bb]Jesus with truth that they [Cm]could not fade
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Ab]Some were convinced by [Eb]the words he had spoken
[Bb]Others would not believe and the [Cm]truth was broken
[Ab]They disagreed [Eb]and began to leave
[Bb]With heated arguments [G]in the heat
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]The Holy Spir[Eb]it spoke through Isaiah's pen
[Bb]You will listen and listen but [Cm]never understand
[Ab]Hearts have grown dull and [Eb]eyes are shut tight
[Bb]So they may not see or [Cm]hear the light
[Ab]God's salva[Eb]tion is sent to the Gentiles [Bb]now
And they will listen to the voice of the [Cm]vow
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Ab]Two whole years [Eb]in his rented place
Pro[Bb]claiming the kingdom with [Cm]boldness and grace
[Ab]Without hindrance [Eb]he taught the Lord
[Bb]With complete boldness un[G]til the very [Cm]end
{end_of_verse}
